2026-10-28  Krishap  <krishapbusiness@gmail.com>

	Run gkey-service as a system service with per-user TPM keys.

	* src/tpm.rs (Blob, UserKey, USER_AUTH_SIZE): New.
	(Tpm::create_user_key, Tpm::with_user_key): New.
	(Tpm::create_signing_key, Tpm::sign, Tpm::seal, Tpm::unseal):
	Create and use objects under a user key.
	* src/keystore.rs: Format version 2, storing the user key and its
	password.  Keystores live in STATE/UID.
	(state_dir, user_dir, DEFAULT_STATE_DIR): New.
	(Keystore::create_credential_key, Keystore::sign): New.
	* src/system.rs: New file.  logind and polkit clients.
	* src/manager.rs: New file.  D-Bus management interface.
	* src/verify.rs: Replace PAM and pinentry with polkit.
	* src/ctap2.rs (Authenticator): Serve the user at the seat.
	(Manage, Job, Jobs, CredentialSummary, Info): New.
	* src/ctaphid.rs (Submit): New trait.
	* src/bin/gkey-service/main.rs: New options --state-dir, --seat
	and --user; remove --keystore, --pam-service and --pinentry.
	* src/bin/gkey/main.rs: Talk to the service over D-Bus; remove
	the init command and the --keystore and --tcti options.
	* data/gkey.service.in: Make it a hardened system unit.
	* data/gkey.sysusers, data/io.github.krishap_s.gkey.policy:
	* data/io.github.krishap_s.Gkey1.conf: New files.
	* data/gkey.pam: Remove.
	* configure.ac, Makefile.in: Install the new files; drop PAM.
	* tests/authenticator.rs: Test isolation between users and the
	user key password.
	* doc/gkey.texi, README.md, INSTALL, DESIGN.md, NEWS: Update.

2026-10-28  Krishap  <krishapbusiness@gmail.com>

	Support Rust 1.80, so that Cargo versions without edition 2024
	support can build gkey.

	* Cargo.toml (rust-version): Set to 1.80.
	* Cargo.lock: Resolve dependency versions compatible with it,
	notably tss-esapi 7.6 and zeroize 1.8.
	* src/uhid.rs (UHIDDevice::create): Allow the deprecation of
	AsyncFd::new.
	* INSTALL: Update the Rust requirement.

2026-10-28  Krishap  <krishapbusiness@gmail.com>

	Implement a TPM backed FIDO2 authenticator.

	* src/tpm.rs: New file.  Storage primary key, signing keys,
	sealing, salted parameter encrypted session.
	* src/keystore.rs: New file.  Credential list encrypted with a
	TPM sealed AES-256-GCM key.
	* src/ctaphid.rs: New file.  CTAPHID transport.
	* src/ctap2.rs: New file.  CTAP 2.0 authenticator.
	* src/verify.rs: New file.  User presence and verification with
	pinentry, PAM, or an external command.
	* src/getopt.rs: New file.  GNU style option parsing.
	* src/uhid.rs: Rewrite without generated bindings.
	* src/bin/gkey-service/main.rs: Serve the authenticator.
	* src/bin/gkey/main.rs: New program to manage credentials.
	* src/ctap2/, src/infra/, src/utils/: Remove.
	* tests/authenticator.rs, tests/fido2-client.py:
	* tests/run-tests.sh, examples/socket-authenticator.rs: New files.
	* doc/gkey.texi: New manual.
	* data/: systemd user unit, udev rule, PAM configuration and
	kernel module list.
	* configure.ac, Makefile.in: Check for tpm2-tss and PAM; provide
	the standard GNU targets.
	* LICENSE: Rename to COPYING.
	* AUTHORS, INSTALL, NEWS, ChangeLog: New files.
	* Cargo.toml: Replace uhid-virt and passkey-transports with
	tss-esapi, ciborium and aes-gcm.
	* default.nix, flake.nix: Build with tpm2-tss and PAM.
